    "title": "Where to watch the Dodgers vs. Blue Jays in World Series rematch for free tonight",
    "text": "Toronto Blue Jays pitcher Trey Yesavage throws against the Los Angeles Dodgers during the first inning in Game 5 of baseball's World Series, Wednesday, Oct. 29, 2025, in Los Angeles. (AP Photo/Brynn Anderson)APIf you purchase a product through a link on our site, we may receive compensation.By Jenna Malinowski | JMalinowski@mlive.comThe Toronto Blue Jays and the Los Angeles Dodgers will face off tonight in a rematch of the 2025 World Series. The Dodgers ultimately won the title in seven games. Fans can catch the action from Rogers Centre on Fox Sports 1 at 7 p.m. ET, with streaming options available through Fubo, DirecTV Stream and Sling. New customers can score free trials and first-month discounts through Fubo and DirecTV Stream.Streaming OptionsFubo: Fans can watch Fox Sports 1 with Fubo’s Pro plan, which includes a total of 213 channels. This plan comes with local channels such as ABC, CBS and Fox and can be watched on up to 10 screens at once. DirecTV Stream: Fox Sports 1 is also available through all three of DirecTV Stream’s packages. Its Entertainment plan offers new subscribers a five-day free trial and $35 off for the first month. Sling: Another option to stream tonight’s game is with Sling’s Select plan, which starts at $19.99 per month and includes sports channels such as Fox Sports 1, Fox Sports 2 and NFL Network. MLBToronto Blue Jays vs. Los Angeles DodgersWhen: Monday, April 6, 2026Where: Rogers Centre, Toronto, ONTime: 7 p.m. ETChannel: Fox Sports 1Where to watch the Golden State Warriors vs. Los Angeles Clippers NBA play-in game free streamHow to watch Orlando Magic vs. Philadelphia 76ers NBA play-in game for free tonightHow to watch the Detroit Tigers vs. Kansas City Royals tonight for free without cableJenna is a sports commerce writer for MLive.com. She writes about how to stream and get ticket deals for your favorite sporting events and where you can find gear for the Detroit Tigers, the Detroit Red Wings,...",
